{"step_index":303,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-10T19:46:29Z","thinking":"**Analyzing User Pharmacy Search Queries**\n\nThe user's input indicates that autocomplete suggestions for medicines are working as expected. Observed the user is searching for pharmacies in `Mirpur, Dhaka` with the medicines `seclo` or `napa`. Initial hypothesis: the issue is not with the autocomplete but with the pharmacy search itself.\n\n\n**Investigating Pharmacy Search Behavior**\n\nObserved that the system returns \"No Pharmacies Found\" because the search criteria (`Mirpur` area) and pharmacy names don't match exactly in the database, due to registration location constraints. The frontend searches only trigger on Enter key press, causing live search to fail when typing. This issue presents an opportunity to provide a better user experience by allowing a live search that triggers automatically as the user types, and providing automatic suggestions for pharmacies, even when there are no results matching the selected area. Backend fallback search across all areas will need to occur to provide results if no pharmacies are found in selected area.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"view_file","args":{"AbsolutePath":"C:\\Users\\User\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\medcheck-bd\\client\\price.html","toolAction":"View price.html","toolSummary":"View price.html"}}]}
